<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Widget strings.

  Values are labels and fragments; anything with a number in it is formatted in
  `WidgetPresenter` with the device locale, so a locale's decimal separator is
  decided by the locale and not by a positional placeholder.

  The vocabulary shared with the iOS Widget is taken from
  `ios/DPIPWidgets/Localizable.xcstrings` (`widget.stale`, `widget.humidity`, …)
  so the two platforms' Widgets say the same thing in the same language. The
  strings that only exist here — the degradation notices, the configuration
  screen, the preview sample — are authored in this file and in the four
  translations beside it.

  The app's in-app language picker does not reach here: a home-screen Widget is
  rendered with the system locale, which is why every locale the app ships is
  covered by `values-<locale>/` rather than left to English.
-->
<resources>
